  "id": "COMPOUND:33673 - PROTEIN:5858",
  "verbalization": "Petroraspailyne B1 is implicated in the biological activity of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol and [6,7-dihydroxy-8-(hydroxymethyl)-4,18-dimethyl-14-[(1Z,3E)-nona-1,3-dienyl]-5-oxo-16-prop-1-en-2-yl-9,13,15,19-tetraoxahexacyclo[12.4.1.01,11.02,6.08,10.012,16]nonadec-3-en-17-yl] benzoate. All these compounds ultimately target KB, suggesting a consistent pathway where Petroraspailyne B1 acts as a mediator in the interaction with KB. The evidence supports a mechanism where Petroraspailyne B1 is a key player in the targeting of KB through its interaction with Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a common target across multiple compounds. This suggests that the relationship between Petroraspailyne B1 and KB may be mediated through a shared target, Microtubule-associated protein 1B, and the evidence is consistent across different compounds that share this target. The integration of these paths highlights a potential mechanism where Petroraspailyne B1 influences KB through a central molecular interaction, reinforcing the notion of a shared biological role.",
